/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The reverse is also possible: downloading a file from a remote system to our local one. Suppose the remote system has a file called documents.txt in /home/ubuntu/, and we want to copy it back to our local machine as notes.txt. The command would look like this: scp ubuntu@192.168.1.30:/home/ubuntu/documents.txt notes.txt)
/E (The reverse is also possible: downloading a file from a remote system to our local one. Suppose the remote system has a file called documents.txt in /home/ubuntu/, and we want to copy it back to our local machine as notes.txt. The command would look like this: scp ubuntu@192.168.1.30:/home/ubuntu/documents.txt notes.txt)
/Pg 78 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
